    <div class="article-header-content px-0 col-11 col-md-10 mx-auto py-md-5 py-4 ">
        <h1 class="fs-1 article-header-title mb-3">
            2026 GENERAL ELECTION
        </h1>
        <div class="article-header-footer d-flex flex-wrap gap-1 align-items-center articles-category">
            <span id="article-header-tag"
                  class="article-badge badge rounded-pill text-border-primary fw-semibold text-truncate me-2 ">
                News Releases
            </span>
            <span id="article-header-date" class="fst-italic opacity-75">
                Posted on October 13, 2026 
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

        </div>

        <div class="my-4 col-11 m-auto">
            <!-- Article Content -->
            <div class="article-content redesign-text fr-view">
    <p><p data-pasted="true"><strong>CORINTH, TX, October 13, 2026</strong> – The City of Corinth will host the General Election on Tuesday, November 3, at Corinth City Hall, 3300 Corinth Parkway. Registered voters will have the opportunity to cast ballots on local, state, and federal matters. Residents are encouraged to take note of the following important dates and information for the upcoming election.</p><p><strong>Early Voting Schedule</strong></p><p>Early voting is available at any Denton County voting location. A full list of early voting sites can be found at <a href="https://www.votedenton.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">VoteDenton.gov</a>. The early voting schedule at Corinth City Hall is as follows.</p><ul style="list-style-type: disc;"><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Monday, October 19 – Friday, October 23: 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Saturday, October 24: 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Sunday, October 25: 11 a.m. to 5 p.m.</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Monday, October 26 – Friday, October 30: 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.</li></ul><p><strong>Election Day Voting</strong></p><p>Election day is Tuesday, November 3, from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. Voting locations are determined by precinct. Voter information, including precinct numbers, and a sample ballot can be found at <a href="https://www.votedenton.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">VoteDenton.gov</a>.</p><ul style="list-style-type: disc;"><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Precinct 2071 – Antioch Christian Fellowship, 2020 Post Oak Dr. – Fellowship Hall</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Precinct 2072 – American Eagle Harley Davidson, 5920 S. I35 E. – Showroom Floor</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Precinct 2073 – Corinth City Hall, 3300 Corinth Parkway – Lobby</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Precinct 3160 – Lake Sharon Community Church, 2650 Oakmont Drive – Fire Place Room</li></ul><p><strong>Voter Registration Eligibility</strong></p><p>To confirm eligibility or to view a sample ballot, visit the <a href="https://www.votedenton.gov/voter-information/voter-lookup/#VoterEligibilitySearch" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Denton County Voter Eligibility</a> page and enter your full name and birthdate. All voters are encouraged to verify their registration status and polling locations before Election Day.</p><p><strong>Required Identification</strong></p><p>Texas law requires voters to present one of the following acceptable forms of photo identification:</p><ul style="list-style-type: disc;"><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Texas Driver License issued by the Texas Department of Public Safety (DPS)</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Texas Personal Identification Card  issued by DPS</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Texas Election Identification Certificate issued by DPS</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">Texas Handgun License issued by DPS </li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">United States Military Identification Card containing the person’s photograph</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">United States Citizenship Certificate containing the person’s photograph</li><li style="margin-left: 24px;">United States Passport (book or card)</li></ul><p>If a voter cannot present an acceptable form of identification, a supporting form of identification may be submitted along with a "Reasonable Impediment Declaration." More information on Voter ID requirements is available from the  <a href="https://www.votetexas.gov/voting/need-id.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Texas Secretary of State</a>.</p><p>For additional election information, contact the City Secretary at (940) 498-3242.</p></p>
</div>



